[{"id":"VRCE-5-60-1","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":1,"english":"Thereupon Hanumān, the foremost of the monkeys, spoke to them, saying.-\"O monkeys, do youundisturbed drink honey. I shall myself thwart them who will obstruct you.\"","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-1"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060001","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c775a61142e6c37247a2185f2faa1f495da912dd7b5522fca6d6a26cf4f18582","compact":"d67cd7190709745b781efdb8fe9ca69ab74932c0dbba9d58ef9be261800e9959","nasal":"d67cd7190709745b781efdb8fe9ca69ab74932c0dbba9d58ef9be261800e9959"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-2","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":2,"english":"Hearing his works, Angada, the best of the monkeys, delighted, said-'Drink honey, O monkeys, we must follow Hanumān's advice, who has already been crowned with success. We must follow him even if he lead us to an unworthy action, what of this which is most becoming?\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060002","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"626276ce98b3531e85ebd57a3cca1d37ca10a2e89cdcc113bc7bbc54e0621c80","compact":"706c4298f3806f1c99875d89651de3dd7d477d0360764bba19e6b9437056b50a","nasal":"3af8295f99b8c18582cd4d965968d787fdb1a74352b37acee514632fcc72989b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-3","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":3,"english":"Hearing his works, Angada, the best of the monkeys, delighted, said-'Drink honey, O monkeys, we must follow Hanumān's advice, who has already been crowned with success. We must follow him even if he lead us to an unworthy action, what of this which is most becoming?\"","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-2"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060003","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"c563c65c18ca281525dd6d25b357e8d9be08aa14196ab0237373ddda9192bde8","compact":"9166a1ecd1da8bb6f2b87792a3a4c98cd4846c0970325c02c8f50d38f6225cdd","nasal":"3f69d2564eb76f80da9deeefd7863b599a2df76f65b78e133805e5fbd2c2cd4d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-4","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":4,"english":"Hearing these words from Angada, the leading monkeys attained to an excess of delight and eulogized him again and again.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.925,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-3"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060004","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9936c88176cef9eea1fed8f29dc1a079ec61f255a06ed9505b7337e7cfba79f","compact":"6e549e05139429fd862fabdb0a6a1d0077d5e24f1cb0a8cc1590807c2c259ccf","nasal":"06655f80d68c5abc60f9b62b437c2106f9bb0e730e7288f39ada5fa0ce317feb"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-5","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":5,"english":"saw And adoring Angada-their prince, those monkeys proceeded by the way leading to the Madhuvana like to trees carried by a stream.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.898,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-4"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060005","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b83a0054f55f1126d48165fb0c29de5a80206ae8022a194e5514fde0bf0348c6","compact":"6007aaed62744ee7d4959dbc0ba3251722399a6dffe2dddc81570e8d7469937b","nasal":"3284f8d222a95797b69773765c0fb166e1f1426a9e588f4737f3ce7a22eb91b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-6","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":6,"english":"And entering that orchard they forcibly attacked the waiters there. Hanuman Maithili, and others heard of her from him-and those monkeys,-renouncing all fear in consequence and obtaining permission, drank honey and feasted on various sweet fruits.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.725,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-5"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060006","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b3944e55ac95bb27e103bab9151b5c7c2a0793dc529c332228f68d22cad0dab2","compact":"497f38f3426880ffe88dcfeb3a03bd284c3e4fca6fab5988b5e3162645e1c5a6","nasal":"497f38f3426880ffe88dcfeb3a03bd284c3e4fca6fab5988b5e3162645e1c5a6"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":7,"english":"And they, given to the drinking of honey, attacking the guards who were approaching by hundreds gave them a sound beating. Some monkeys, collecting honey with their hands measuring a Droņa, (In common use a measure of thirty-two seers of rather more than sixty four Ibs. quadrupeds) drank it; others collecting themselves delightedly into a band spoiled it; while other yellow-coloured monkeys drank and sprinkled it And some, being beside themselves with intoxication, struck others with the remaining quantity, while others waited at the foot of the trees, holding their boughs.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.455,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"6abf5b723621516c5fda6279246b709081729d51e6ed28cf161953e59cc3a221","compact":"edfa0273d281aa98586b48ebdccec76e88765f98052804572bc390de4a485cff","nasal":"e412cc4379dc9ae530e247eb088e239d2e798f2154417a8aeac483811aa1062d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":8,"english":"And they, given to the drinking of honey, attacking the guards who were approaching by hundreds gave them a sound beating. Some monkeys, collecting honey with their hands measuring a Droņa, (In common use a measure of thirty-two seers of rather more than sixty four Ibs. quadrupeds) drank it; others collecting themselves delightedly into a band spoiled it; while other yellow-coloured monkeys drank and sprinkled it And some, being beside themselves with intoxication, struck others with the remaining quantity, while others waited at the foot of the trees, holding their boughs.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.778,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-6"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"fd53d88da910a26701ed61122de4ffa95886ca2d144e67b973dc0607e67829f4","compact":"2626f7cf37c14cd885da38d2a0ba931ebf48a1d7658ddb73b9c2b88e6cd46600","nasal":"4fdb2103590fbb92e0d3960c6e0fc3791e3678e16661282648ce13c182a1a11c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":9,"english":"And they, given to the drinking of honey, attacking the guards who were approaching by hundreds gave them a sound beating. Some monkeys, collecting honey with their hands measuring a Droņa, (In common use a measure of thirty-two seers of rather more than sixty four Ibs. quadrupeds) drank it; others collecting themselves delightedly into a band spoiled it; while other yellow-coloured monkeys drank and sprinkled it And some, being beside themselves with intoxication, struck others with the remaining quantity, while others waited at the foot of the trees, holding their boughs. And some, being exhausted with drinking, spread leaves and laid themselves thereon-and some being drunk and delighted struck others down in mad fury. And some lost their steps. Some roared and some delightedly set up the music of the birds.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.437,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-6","DUTT-5-62-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskri