,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":12,"english":"And some, being exhausted with drinking, spread leaves and laid themselves thereon-and some being drunk and delighted struck others down in mad fury. And some lost their steps. Some roared and some delightedly set up the music of the birds. Some of the monkeys, inebriate with honey, slept on the earth; some laughed at others impudently and some cried aloud.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.467,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-7","DUTT-5-62-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"46813c5a91e54b89c25c92894845daaaf2226de881721eac9c15772df539d4eb","compact":"927d5ff664520c0a55ba8da71e69a4cdea5c078f448ab68f297f3bc56d4cb974","nasal":"9a5f0a3f8af9c0e84e1b0e40c1cc61930e27740e761f420743432407208319f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":13,"english":"Some spoke contrary to what they had doneand others put a different construction thereon. And all the waiters of the garden and the servants of Dadhimukha, were repressed by those terrible monkeys with censure and thrown up in the shy by their Knee-joints. And terrified, they fled to different directions.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-62-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5060013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e05489e43bd0d593498f10a521a9a46f45c648261806bceb1d6a2043562c5512","compact":"a3a08a247790eb9d5c9a2a5d4fbdd4ec3dcc490747083f828a63cc6a92db6e23","nasal":"a3a08a247790eb9d5c9a2a5d4fbdd4ec3dcc490747083f828a63cc6a92db6e23"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-60-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":60,"verse":14,"english":"Some spoke contrary to what they had doneand others put a different construction thereon. And all the waiters of the 